    "result": "The vault is initialized, and I didn't run `init.mjs`. Both existing files are byte-for-byte unchanged, confirmed by hash before and after for `index.md` and `_templates/authored-note.md`.\n\n**Why I skipped `init.mjs`.** It copies the bundled `_templates/` folder recursively with no overwrite guard. Your `_templates/authored-note.md` differs from the bundled one, so it would have been replaced. Instead I created only the missing files, following the missing-only path in the initialization reference.\n\n**What I created:**\n- **Folders:** `raw/clippings`, `wiki/{sources,entities,concepts,syntheses,authored}`, `moc` and `log`.\n- **Root files:** `log.md`, `.gitignore`, `vault-schema.md`, `stale.base` and `log.base`.\n- **Templates:** `authored-backlog-item.md`, `authored-decision.md`, `concept-note.md`, `source-note.md` and `task-map.md`, all in `_templates/`.\n- **Operation log:** `log/2026-11-02-155451-relink-initialize-vault.md`.\n\n**Checks:**\n- **Health:** `health.mjs --json` exited 0 with status `empty` and 0 defects. There is no content yet, so this says nothing about factual health.\n- **Operation:** I opened and closed relink operation `11f2032ffad9d878` with the log recorded.\n- **Publication:** This is local-only. The vault isn't a Git repository, so `op-commit` had nothing to commit. I didn't create a repository or remote.\n\n**Not done:**\n- The Obsidian setup: open the folder as a vault, check it with `obsidian.mjs vaults`, and import `templates/webclipper-template.json` into Web Clipper.\n- The semantic search index. It isn't built; `index-embed.mjs` would build it.\n- I made no changes to the plugin, caches or global settings, installed no dependencies and configured no app.",
